    <summary>A simple, lightweight markdown editor offering all the features you could ever need.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
nibeditor is a markdown editor that shows the formatting instead of the syntax. Headings,
bold, lists, tables, code and math are styled in place as you type, so there is no split
pane and no preview pane to keep in sync.

Notes are plain `.md` files on disk, opened and saved where you put them, with no library or
vault to import into. Themes are single CSS files dropped into the config folder, every edit
is snapshotted so a bad change can be undone later, and the same editor runs in the browser
at [nibeditor.com](https://nibeditor.com).

### Features

* Inline preview - the document is the preview, not a second pane
* Plain Markdown files, no proprietary store
* CSS themes, dropped straight into the config folder
* Automatic snapshots of every note before it is overwritten
* Runs on Windows, macOS, Linux, and in the browser

### Notes on this package

This package installs the machine-wide MSI build, so nibeditor lands in `Program Files`
and is available to every user on the machine. x64 and ARM64 are both supported; 32-bit
Windows is not. The MSI is not code-signed.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/lxorb/nibeditor/releases/tag/v0.13.0</releaseNotes>
